2026-08-27  ICBR RC-wise susceptibility: low-denominator cells

WHAT I DID
Parsed all six pathogen sheets of ICBR_RC_Wise_Susceptibility__2_.xlsx
and listed every cell with fewer than 10 isolates tested.
Output: ICBR_low_N_cells.xlsx

RESULT
3,276 cells total. 260 have N < 10 and are excluded.

DECISIONS
- Exclude the individual cell where N < 10. Keep the centre, year and
  pathogen otherwise.
  Reason: excluding whole centres would systematically remove newer
  centres, which are mostly in under-represented regions.
- N is the denominator printed inside the cell (isolates tested against
  that antibiotic at that centre), not the column-header N, which is
  the national total for the year.

LIMITATION
Low-N cells cluster in smaller centres (RIMS Imphal, Apollo Chennai,
Artemis Gurugram) and rarer organisms (P. mirabilis, E. cloacae).
Exclusion therefore thins the northeast more than Maharashtra or Delhi.

OPEN
RC number to institution key is published only in the 2021 report
(Figure (i), p.5). Institution names for other years are provisional.
